cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software
title: "NexClamp: Perturbation-Battery Testing for Behavioural Preservation in Computational Neuron Models"
abstract: >-
  NexClamp is a research framework for detecting silent behavioural drift in computational
  neuron models written in NeuroML v2 and LEMS: edits that leave a model valid, runnable and
  passing its canonical test while changing how it responds to other current-clamp stimuli.
  It combines current-clamp protocol batteries, eFEL electrophysiology features, tolerances
  calibrated by numerical refinement, controlled single-fault mutants, greedy protocol
  selection and held-out evaluation. Pre-release software; no scientific results yet.
